---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="Changelog"
  description="Release history for AI Blog Writer with Sources, the source-backed AI draft plugin for WordPress."
  schema={[breadcrumbNode([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Changelog', path: '/changelog/' }])]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Changelog</p>
      <h1>Changelog</h1>

      <h2 id="1-2-1">1.2.1</h2>
      <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-10-06">6 October 2026</time>.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Fix: no more "Translation loading for the luis-rita-ai-blog-writer domain was triggered too early" notice on WordPress 6.7 and later when debugging is on</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="1-2-0">1.2.0</h2>
      <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-10-06">6 October 2026</time>.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The plugin's screens mention the optional <a href="/pricing/">AI Blog Writer Pro</a> add-on where it helps: New article, finished drafts, Settings and the Plugins screen. Each mention can be dismissed, they disappear once the add-on is installed, and nothing is sent anywhere</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="1-1-0">1.1.0</h2>
      <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-10-02">2 October 2026</time>.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Other plugins can now extend AI Blog Writer with extra brief fields, automatic research, post-draft checks and more SEO integrations. Nothing changes until such a plugin is installed</li>
        <li>After your third completed draft, a one-time prompt asks for a WordPress.org review. Either answer hides it for good</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="1-0-1">1.0.1</h2>
      <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-09-30">30 September 2026</time>.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Fix: editors can now save writer profiles by linking them to an existing Author account. Administrators can also create a new author account or link an existing one</li>
        <li>New author accounts get hyphenated logins instead of logins with spaces</li>
        <li>Documentation and Support links on the plugin's row in the Plugins screen</li>
        <li>The plugin's homepage link now points to sourcedwriter.com</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="1-0-0">1.0.0</h2>
      <p class="meta">
        Initial public release on <a href="https://wordpress.org/plugins/luis-rita-ai-blog-writer/">WordPress.org</a>,
        <time datetime="2026-09-30">30 September 2026</time>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Bring-your-own-key drafting with OpenAI, Anthropic, Google and xAI models</li>
        <li>Delegated and Guided workflows with user-supplied sources, outline review and provenance</li>
        <li>Writer profiles linked to WordPress author accounts</li>
        <li>Optional Rank Math metadata integration</li>
        <li>Usage tracking with optional estimated cost ceilings</li>
        <li>Retention cleanup, privacy export and erasure, and opt-in data removal on uninstall</li>
        <li>Single-site and network activation support</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
